# PHASE 7 — Graph, Preset & Canvas Storage Normalization

**Read `00 - START HERE` first for ground rules (stack, design language, "never do this" list) — they still apply in full.** This phase does not depend on Phase 5. It does depend on Phase 6 (the rich `FieldDef`/config shape) being in place, which it is.

This phase touches **only** the files listed in §2 (Scope) plus the specific call sites named in §5. Do not restyle, refactor, or "improve" anything else you notice while you're in these files — if you spot something unrelated, note it in a "found but not fixed" list at the end of your session instead of fixing it inline.

Still frontend-only. Still no backend. This phase does not add a database or an API route. What it does is make the **existing** `localStorage`/Zustand data shape internally consistent, so that (a) a strategy graph is byte-for-byte identical wherever it travels inside the app, and (b) that same shape can be handed to a Postgres/Prisma schema later with no redesign.

