### 5.2 `duplicateBot`

Already spreads the whole `source` object today, which — once `Bot.graph` replaces the four loose fields — still isn't quite right, because a plain spread shares array references with the original bot. Fix it to explicitly clone:

```ts
duplicateBot: (id) => {
  const source = get().bots.find((b) => b.id === id)
  if (!source) return null
  const graph = cloneGraph(source.graph)
  const copy: Bot = {
    ...source,
    id: slugId('bot'),
    name: `${source.name} copy`,
    status: 'draft',
    createdAt: nowISO(),
    updatedAt: nowISO(),
    visibility: 'private',
    runIds: [],
    graph,
    versions: [{ id: slugId('v'), label: 'v1', createdAt: nowISO(), note: `Duplicated from ${source.name}`, nodeCount: graph.nodes.length, graph: cloneGraph(graph) }],
  }
  set({ bots: [copy, ...get().bots] })
  return copy
}
```

### 5.3 `saveGraph`

Simplify to always take a full `BotGraph` rather than separate `nodes`/`edges`/optional `annotations`:

```ts
saveGraph: (id, graph) =>
  set({
    bots: get().bots.map((b) => (b.id === id ? { ...b, graph, updatedAt: nowISO() } : b)),
  }),
```

Every existing call site of `saveGraph(id, nodes, edges, annotations)` must be updated to pass a single `{ nodes, edges, notes, frames, schemaVersion }` object instead. Grep the whole codebase for `saveGraph(` and fix every call, not just the ones named elsewhere in this document.

### 5.4 `snapshotVersion` — closes bug #6

```ts
snapshotVersion: (id, note) =>
  set({
    bots: get().bots.map((b) =>
      b.id === id
        ? {
            ...b,
            updatedAt: nowISO(),
            versions: [
              { id: slugId('v'), label: `v${b.versions.length + 1}`, createdAt: nowISO(), note, nodeCount: b.graph.nodes.length, graph: cloneGraph(b.graph) },
              ...b.versions,
