```

Note `cloneGraph`, not `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))` — cloning gives every note/frame/node/edge in the snapshot its own fresh IDs, which matters once notes/frames actually get captured (previously this used raw deep-copy since it only handled nodes/edges; now that notes/frames are included, use the same clone utility as everywhere else for consistency, since a version snapshot is conceptually "fork this moment in time," even though it's not user-facing as a fork).

### 5.5 Marketplace publish flow — closes bug #5, the critical one

In `app/app/marketplace/publish/[botId]/page.tsx`, `handlePublish()` currently builds `publishedItem` with no graph at all. Fix:

```ts
const handlePublish = () => {
  const publishedItem: PublishedPreset = {
    id: slugId('preset'),
    name: name.trim() || bot.name,
    clones: 0,
    revenue: 0,
    rating: 5.0,
