This alone is necessary but not sufficient — `PublishedPreset` (creator-dashboard-facing) and `Preset` (public marketplace browsing/forking-facing) are still two different types today. Decide and implement one of these two approaches, and document your choice in a code comment at both type definitions:

- **Approach A (recommended, simpler):** make `Preset` the single public-facing type, and have `publishPreset` actually push into the same list the public `/marketplace` pages read from (today likely a separate `PRESETS`/`MARKETPLACE_PRESETS` fixture array) — i.e. `PublishedPreset` becomes redundant and creator-dashboard views just filter `Preset[]` down to ones authored by the current user. This is the more correct long-term shape (a published bot *is* a marketplace preset, not two separate records that happen to share a name) and sets up cleanly for a future backend where this is obviously one table.
