## 8. Schema-mismatch safety net

Because `schemaVersion` now exists, add one small piece of defensive UI: if `useHydrated()` loads a `Bot` whose `graph.schemaVersion` is less than `CURRENT_GRAPH_SCHEMA_VERSION` and `migrateGraph` had to actually change something (not just pass through), show a one-time `toast.info` on that bot's page: *"This bot's canvas layout was upgraded to the current format."* This isn't scope creep — it's the honest UX consequence of introducing versioning, and it's the pattern you'll want later when a real backend migration touches user data.

